# Docker Development

**Never run `bundle`, `rails`, or `rspec` directly on the WSL host.**
Use the matching Compose service.

## Services

| Service | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `app` | Rails, Bundler, RSpec, rake, rails console |
| `frontend` | npm, Vite, TypeScript build |
| `postgres` | DB (host port `36000` → container `5432`) |

## Commands

```bash
# Backend
docker compose exec app bundle install
docker compose exec app bundle exec rails db:migrate
docker compose exec app bundle exec rails c
docker compose exec app bundle exec rspec
docker compose exec app bundle exec rspec spec/models/word_spec.rb

# One-off (no running app container)
docker compose run --rm app bundle exec rails db:test:prepare

# Frontend
docker compose exec frontend npm install
docker compose exec frontend npm run build
docker compose exec frontend npm run dev
```

## Notes

- Gems install to `/gems` volume inside `app`
- `.env` provides `POSTGRES_*` vars for containers
- If `spec/` files are root-owned after `rails generate`, fix with:
  `docker compose exec -u root app chown -R 1000:1000 /app/spec`
